    {
      "id": "plan_agent_edited_node_hints",
      "text": "Improvement 1: transient agent-edited node highlights\nWhen an agent/sync update changes nodes, temporarily highlight those nodes in the canvas until the user hovers over each highlighted node. This is only an editor-local hint and should not write any backend state.",
      "tags": [
        "frontend-only",
        "implemented",
        "improvement",
        "plan",
        "ux"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2480,
          "y": 250
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_agent_hint_acceptance",
      "text": "Acceptance: edited-node hints\n- Agent-edited nodes visibly pulse/glow or otherwise stand out.\n- Highlight survives until that node is hovered.\n- No new resource schema/backend operation.\n- User edits do not create false agent-edited hints.\n- Resource switching/reload clears stale hints safely.",
      "tags": [
        "acceptance",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 3318.9711227953367,
          "y": 195.29720865227745
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_agent_hint_scope",
      "text": "Scope for edited-node hints\nUse editor-local state such as editedHintNodeIDs and node data flags. Clear a node hint on pointer hover via ArchitectureNodeView onEditedHintSeen. Detect external/agent node changes during resource sync rather than adding a saved graph field.",
      "tags": [
        "candidate",
        "frontend-only",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2898,
          "y": 266
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_drop_connection_acceptance",
      "text": "Acceptance: drop-to-create-node\n- Preview appears only for a dangling connection over empty canvas.\n- Dropping on an existing compatible handle keeps normal connect behavior.\n- Dropping empty creates a default node and one edge.\n- Escape/cancel/pointer cancel removes preview.\n- Undo removes both created node and edge together.",
      "tags": [
        "acceptance",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 3317.75210915141,
          "y": 553.5415321131238
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_drop_connection_create_node",
      "text": "Improvement 2: drop dangling connection to create node\nWhen the user drags a connection from a node and releases on empty canvas, show a hollow preview hint that dropping now will create a new node already connected to the source node.",
      "tags": [
        "implemented",
        "improvement",
        "plan",
        "ux"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2483.0779878805542,
          "y": 542.0947555426015
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_drop_connection_scope",
      "text": "Scope for drop-to-create-node\nUse React Flow connection start/end state in ArchitectureEditor. While dragging over empty pane, render a hollow node/card preview at the prospective drop position. On drop, create node.create plus edge.create operations in one commit batch.",
      "tags": [
        "candidate",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2898,
          "y": 506
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_improvements_overview",
      "text": "Plan: Graph editor interaction improvements\nThree frontend UX improvements: transient hints for agent-edited nodes, drop-to-create-node from a dangling connection, and separated connection anchor points for crowded rectangular wires.",
      "tags": [
        "improvement",
        "plan",
        "ux"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2238.9395577242603,
          "y": -58.25975433341344
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_separated_connection_points",
      "text": "Improvement 3: separate crowded connection points\nWhen multiple lines connect to one node, offset each exact edge endpoint along the selected side according to source/target ordering so rectangular wires are easier to distinguish and drag off individually.",
      "tags": [
        "implemented",
        "improvement",
        "plan",
        "ux"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2487.9999999999995,
          "y": 803.4234747268662
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_separated_points_acceptance",
      "text": "Acceptance: separated endpoints\n- Multiple edges on the same node side no longer overlap at one point.\n- Existing edges remain reconnectable/disconnectable by dragging their visible endpoint.\n- New incoming connections still target the normal side handles.\n- Rectangular wires become easier to trace.\n- No saved schema changes unless a later design explicitly requires persisted anchor offsets.",
      "tags": [
        "acceptance",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 3305.5619727121475,
          "y": 910.5668419300439
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_separated_points_scope",
      "text": "Scope for separated endpoints\nKeep user-visible connection handles conceptually on the four node sides for new drag targets, but render existing edge endpoints with per-edge offsets near the side. This is a rendering/interaction aid, not a graph data-model change.",
      "tags": [
        "candidate",
        "frontend-only",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2898,
          "y": 787.0167676620473
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_shared_constraints",
      "text": "Shared constraints for all three improvements\nPrefer local UI state and typed operation batches. Do not add backend fields for visual hints. Keep changes in architecture-editor.react.tsx, architecture-node.react.tsx, architecture-edge.react.tsx, model.ts, editor-commands.ts, and CSS unless deeper runtime state is truly needed.",
      "tags": [
        "frontend-only",
        "guide",
        "plan"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2484.718658587036,
          "y": 1076.236888856504
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan_verification_improvements",
      "text": "Verification plan for improvements\nAdd or update focused tests around editor-commands operation batches, selection/connection state, edit-hint behavior, model mapping, and style snapshots where practical. Run packages/app focused tests and bun typecheck for touched contracts.",
      "tags": [
        "acceptance",
        "plan",
        "verify"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "position": {
          "x": 2897.371836272885,
          "y": 1064.2238828618226
        }
      }
    },
